ow the expected margin.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings.", "Incumbent Steven Horsford (D) is running."]}, "overview": "Steven Horsford, the Democratic incumbent, seeks another term in a district that leans slightly Democratic. He has raised about $4.1 million and holds a large cash advantage over Republican Cody Whipple, a small-town rancher who has raised roughly $1.2 million with limited cash remaining. The two independent candidates show no meaningful fundraising or outside support.\n\nPublic polling is absent, but ten expert ratings converge on a Democratic edge, most calling the race Likely Democratic and a few rating it Safe or Solid. Betting markets give Horsford roughly a 95 percent chance of winning. His incumbency, financial dominance, and the district's lean point to a comfortable but not entirely risk-free margin. Whipple's focus on border security and election integrity has drawn local coverage but little outside spending so far.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9628, "margin": 12.37}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9577, "margin": 12.4}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9584, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9615, "margin": 12.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9427, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9481, "margin": 12.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9627, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9594, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9636, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9567, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.9624, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.96, "margin": 12.3}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.9555, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.9434, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.9455, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.941, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem"